{%- comment -%}
!!!! IMPORTANT !!!!
Please read this before proceeding, to understand what sitemap captures,
and how it behaves, etc.

Reference: https://www.sitemaps.org/protocol.html

= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =
# PAGE and SITEMAP REQUIREMENTS & GUIDELINES # 
= = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = = =
1. Pages should have: (Page YAML example below)
    a. searchable: "true"
    b. and 'metadata' of search_engine_visibility: "true" 

IF one of these is "false" or not set, page will not be included in sitemap.

2. Sitemap nodes / fields
    a. <loc> Location / Page URL: Full path page URL
    b. <changefreq> Page Change Frequency: Default = 'monthly'
            Values: [always, hourly, daily, weekly, monthly, yearly, never]
    c. <priority> Page Priority: Default = 1.0
            Values: [0.0 to 1.0]
    d. <lastmod> Page Last Modified: Page 'updated_at'
            Format: 'YYYY-MM-DD' in pOS {{ __ | date: '%Y-%m-%d' }}

Example page YAML config:
---
slug: services
layout: modules/ins_template_website/dynamic_cms_1col
searchable: "true"
max_deep_level: 2
metadata: {
page_title: "Services | Insites",
meta_title: "Services | Insites",
description: "Services | Insites Demo Description",
canonical_url: "",
status: "published",
search_engine_visibility: "true",
sitemap_priority: 0.5, ## primary order (ASC)
sitemap_order: 3, ## secondary order (ASC)
sitemap_changefreq: "monthly"
}
---

3. Order / Sequence
- pages are sorted by page.metadata :
    a. sitemap_priority: Int - Primary sort field (DESC)
    b. sitemap_order: Int - Secondary sort field (ASC)

ALL pages without these metadata fields, will be placed at the bottom, after the 
pages w/ the metadata sort fields.


4. Child / sub pages should be listed after the parent before listing next page(s).
ie. Sitemap structure will look like:
    ...
    - ./blog
        - ./blog/article-1
        - ./blog/article-2
        - ./blog/article-3
    - ./services
        - ./services/a
        - ./services/b
    - ./contact-us
    - etc..

